{
  "action": "After a standard system update you need to reboot your computer to make all\nthe necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-94284",
    "CVE-2026-94283",
    "CVE-2026-94285",
    "CVE-2026-88806"
  ],
  "description": "Adam Bedard discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled certain XKB keyboard\nmap replies. If a user were tricked into connecting to a malicious X\nserver, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause libx11 to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-88806)\n\nIt was discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled certain X Input Method\n(XIM) messages. If a user were tricked into connecting to a malicious X\nserver, a remote attacker could possibly use these issues to cause libx11\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94283,\nCVE-2026-94284)\n\nIt was discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled converting certain\nmultibyte text. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause libx11\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94285)",
  "id": "USN-8913-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in libx11.",
